where a ∈ L(X × Y, ) is a bounded bilinear form, f ∈ Y ′ := L(Y, ) is a bounded linear form, and 〈·, ·〉Y ′,Y denotes the duality pairing between Y ′ and Y . Alternatively, it is possible to introduce the bounded linear operator A ∈ L(X, Y ′) such that
